{"ref":"BDB, כַּ֫עַשׂ","hw":"כַּ֫עַשׂ","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">כַּ֫עַשׂ</span></big>  <strong>n.m.</strong> (dialectic variation of <span dir=\"rtl\">כַּעַס</span>, only in Jb);—<span dir=\"rtl\">כ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 17:7\" href=\"/Job.17.7\">Jb 17:7</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">כָּ֑עָשׂ</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 5:2\" href=\"/Job.5.2\">Jb 5:2</a>; sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">כַּעְשִׂי</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 6:2\" href=\"/Job.6.2\">Jb 6:2</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">כַּעַשְׂךָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 10:17\" href=\"/Job.10.17\">Jb 10:17</a>;—<br><strong>1.</strong>  <em>vexation, grief</em> of men <a data-ref=\"Job 5:2\" href=\"/Job.5.2\">Jb 5:2</a> (cf. <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 12:16\" href=\"/Proverbs.12.16\">Pr 12:16</a>; <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 27:3\" href=\"/Proverbs.27.3\">27:3</a>), <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 6:2\" href=\"/Proverbs.6.2\">6:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 17:7\" href=\"/Proverbs.17.7\">17:7</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  <em>vexation, anger</em>, of God; c. <span dir=\"rtl\">כַּעַשְׂךָ עִמָּדִי</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 10:17\" href=\"/Job.10.17\">Jb 10:17</a> <em>thine anger with me</em>.","next":"BDB, כַּף","prev":"BDB, כַּ֫עַס"}